# Shell scripts MUST check out with LF, on every platform.
#
# This repo's automation is bash end to end -- `deploy/run-job.sh` and the five scripts
# it wraps -- and a Windows clone under the default `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites them
# to CRLF. Git Bash happens to tolerate CRLF in a script, so that alone is survivable;
# what is not survivable is the ASYMMETRY. Bash strips CR from script SOURCE and not
# from data a script READS, so the scripts keep running while the values they parse
# quietly grow a trailing CR. Measured 2026-09-18: a `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=123:abc` line
# in a CRLF file loads as 8 characters, not 7, and Telegram rejects it while every
# print-out of the token looks correct.
#
# Pinning `eol=lf` is a no-op on Linux and on CI; it exists entirely so a Windows
# checkout of a Linux-shaped repo is not silently different from the repo.
#
# ⚠ It cannot cover `.env`, `config/coins.json` or anything else gitignored -- git
# never sees those files. That is why `deploy/windows/load-env.sh` strips CR itself
# rather than relying on this, and why the strip is the tested behaviour.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf

# PowerShell reads either ending; CRLF is the platform-native choice for a file only
# Windows runs.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Keep diffs and hashing sane on binaries the analytics stack ships.
*.parquet binary
*.duckdb binary
*.db binary
